       "Sydney is closer to the equator, so it moves faster: about one thousand three hundred and ninety. And because it's on the other side of the planet, it's heading in a completely different direction.",
       "So if teleporting kept your old speed, you'd arrive in Sydney moving at roughly two thousand four hundred kilometres an hour, compared with the ground. That's about twice the speed of sound.",
